<h2>Call us first</h2>
<p>If you're in pain or have just had a dental injury, the first step is to call us at <a href="tel:{{ site.phone.telShort }}" data-action="call-emergency">{{ site.phone.display }}</a>. Many "emergencies" can be relieved or stabilized quickly once we see what's going on.</p>

<h2>Common dental emergencies we treat</h2>
<ul class="checklist">
  <li>Severe toothache or throbbing pain</li>
  <li>Broken, chipped, or cracked teeth</li>
  <li>Lost or loose filling, crown, or bridge</li>
  <li>Knocked-out (avulsed) teeth</li>
  <li>Facial or jaw swelling, especially with fever</li>
  <li>Bleeding that won't stop after an injury</li>
  <li>Soft-tissue injuries to the lips, cheeks, or tongue</li>
</ul>

<h2>What we'll do at the visit</h2>
<p>Our first goals are to stop the pain, control any infection, and stabilize the tooth. We may take a focused X-ray, place a temporary restoration or sedative filling, prescribe antibiotics if there's infection, and schedule a follow-up to complete the definitive treatment.</p>

<h2>Until you're seen</h2>
<p>Rinse gently with warm water, use a cold compress on the cheek for swelling, and take over-the-counter pain relief as the label directs. Don't put aspirin directly on the gum. Our guide to <a href="/blog/severe-tooth-pain-after-hours/">severe tooth pain after hours</a> covers what helps and what to avoid, and <a href="/blog/dental-infections-and-swelling/">dental infection and facial swelling</a> lists the warning signs that can't wait.</p>

<h2>Cost of an emergency visit</h2>
<p>Our <strong>$59 emergency visit</strong> covers a focused exam and the X-ray we need, and we see you the same day when a slot is available. Treatment to fix the problem is quoted separately before we start. See <a href="/special-offers/">special offers</a> for terms, and <a href="/insurance-financing/">insurance &amp; financing</a> for payment options.</p>

<h2>Hours and after-hours</h2>
<p>We're open {{ site.hours.display }}. For a dental emergency after hours, <a href="tel:{{ site.phone.telShort }}" data-action="call-emergency">call</a> or <a href="sms:{{ site.phone.tel }}" data-action="call-emergency-text">text</a> {{ site.phone.display }}, or email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>. Dr. Phillips can usually see urgent patients quickly, and same-day extractions are available when a tooth can't be saved.</p>
