<h2>When to skip the dentist and go to the ER</h2>
<p>Go directly to the emergency room (or call 911) if you have significant facial swelling that's affecting your breathing or vision, uncontrolled bleeding, a suspected jaw fracture, or any other life-threatening injury. Dental care can follow afterward once you're stable. Not sure which you need? Read <a href="/blog/emergency-dentist-vs-emergency-room/">emergency dentist vs. emergency room</a>.</p>

<p>If the tooth can't be saved, Dr. Phillips handles extractions here in the office, often the same day. See <a href="/services/tooth-extractions/">tooth extractions</a> and <a href="/services/wisdom-teeth-removal/">wisdom teeth removal</a>. We're at {{ site.address.full }}.</p>

<h2>An emergency dentist near Mesa, Chandler and Scottsdale</h2>
<p>Our office on E Southern Ave in Tempe is a short drive for urgent dental care from Mesa, Chandler, Scottsdale, Gilbert, Ahwatukee and Phoenix. Call ahead so we can have a chair ready when you arrive.</p>
